1
00:00:04,254 --> 00:00:06,005
We have some time
before your appointment

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,005
with the principal.

3
00:00:07,089 --> 00:00:08,630
Do you want to stop anywhere?

4
00:00:08,713 --> 00:00:10,254
No thanks, I'll surprise him

5
00:00:10,338 --> 00:00:12,172
and show up early for a change.

6
00:00:16,422 --> 00:00:17,422
Stop here.

7
00:00:17,464 --> 00:00:18,381
[Kiyotaka] Huh?

8
00:00:18,464 --> 00:00:19,507
Right here?

9
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:20,632
[Satoru] You go on ahead.

10
00:00:20,715 --> 00:00:21,840
(grunts in surprise)

11
00:00:21,924 --> 00:00:23,149
[Kiyotaka] Is this a
test or something?

12
00:00:23,173 --> 00:00:24,673
You're going to hit
me if I drive away

13
00:00:24,757 --> 00:00:26,049
without you, aren't you?

14
00:00:26,132 --> 00:00:28,053
[Satoru] Just what type
of guy do you think I am?

15
00:00:28,133 --> 00:00:29,633
(sighs in relief)

16
00:00:29,716 --> 00:00:32,133
-[Kiyotaka] Okay then.
-(tires screeching)

17
00:00:38,884 --> 00:00:39,967
All right.

18
00:00:40,842 --> 00:00:42,468
(shrieks)

19
00:00:42,551 --> 00:00:45,301
(ground breaking)

20
00:00:48,259 --> 00:00:49,010
I see.

21
00:00:49,094 --> 00:00:50,302
Who are you, then?

22
00:00:51,969 --> 00:00:54,761
(yells battle cry)

23
00:00:58,762 --> 00:01:01,137
(fire roaring)

24
00:01:14,098 --> 00:01:15,847
(chuckles)

25
00:01:15,931 --> 00:01:17,139
That was a whole lot easier

26
00:01:17,222 --> 00:01:20,347
than I expected it was gonna be.

27
00:01:20,430 --> 00:01:21,430
Huh?

28
00:01:27,223 --> 00:01:28,348
[Satoru] So then.

29
00:01:28,431 --> 00:01:31,849
Just who are you calling "easy"?

30
00:01:31,933 --> 00:01:33,016
(groans)

31
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:34,974
What a pain in the ass.

32
00:01:36,058 --> 00:01:38,850
He's a cursed spirit, but
he can communicate clearly.

33
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:43,934
And the sheer amount of
cursed energy he just unleashed.

34
00:01:44,017 --> 00:01:45,976
An unregistered special-grade?

35
00:01:47,684 --> 00:01:50,559
He's likely even stronger
than Sukuna currently is.

36
00:01:51,768 --> 00:01:53,394
Special-grades are
classified as such

37
00:01:53,477 --> 00:01:55,061
because they're special.

38
00:01:55,144 --> 00:01:57,019
Having them pop
up this frequently

39
00:01:57,103 --> 00:01:58,227
throws everything off.

40
00:01:59,103 --> 00:02:00,394
(laughs mockingly)

41
00:02:00,477 --> 00:02:02,978
Aw, don't tell me I
wounded your pride?

42
00:02:04,311 --> 00:02:05,311
No.

43
00:02:05,395 --> 00:02:06,311
(knuckles cracking)

44
00:02:06,395 --> 00:02:08,395
I'm starting to enjoy this.

45
00:02:08,478 --> 00:02:10,813
(chuckles)

46
00:02:13,146 --> 00:02:15,396
(Opening Theme Music)

47
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:32,023
(singing in Japanese)

48
00:03:42,032 --> 00:03:44,950
[Jougo] So you think
this will be fun, do you?

49
00:03:45,033 --> 00:03:47,075
No sense of danger?

50
00:03:47,158 --> 00:03:49,117
None at all?

51
00:03:49,199 --> 00:03:52,118
Did he choose to attack
here in order to avoid people?

52
00:03:53,118 --> 00:03:54,242
No.

53
00:03:54,325 --> 00:03:56,367
He was just making
sure no other sorcerers

54
00:03:56,450 --> 00:03:57,909
could come to back me up.

55
00:03:58,826 --> 00:04:00,119
Ember Insects!

56
00:04:01,493 --> 00:04:03,201
Well, if you're aiming
this attack at me,

57
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:04,493
then you're right.

58
00:04:04,576 --> 00:04:06,410
I'm not feeling any danger.

59
00:04:08,494 --> 00:04:11,369
(ground breaking)

60
00:04:11,452 --> 00:04:13,078
Well!

61
00:04:13,161 --> 00:04:14,787
What if this hits me?

62
00:04:14,870 --> 00:04:17,829
(insect chattering)

63
00:04:19,286 --> 00:04:20,370
Sound?

64
00:04:22,079 --> 00:04:25,038
(insects exploding)

65
00:04:26,538 --> 00:04:29,663
A two-stage attack of
sound and explosions?

66
00:04:29,746 --> 00:04:31,414
That's not bad.

67
00:04:31,497 --> 00:04:34,372
(yells battle cry)

68
00:04:34,455 --> 00:04:36,831
(fire roaring)

69
00:04:37,997 --> 00:04:39,415
And there's more!

70
00:04:41,623 --> 00:04:43,540
(ground breaking)

71
00:04:43,623 --> 00:04:46,249
(fire exploding)

72
00:04:47,332 --> 00:04:49,125
That's all it took?

73
00:04:49,207 --> 00:04:51,582
Obviously, I overestimated him.

74
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:55,500
That human was just as
fragile as the rest of them are.

75
00:04:55,583 --> 00:04:58,000
He wasn't living
any life of truth.

76
00:04:58,084 --> 00:05:00,834
It's all so
nauseatingly repulsive!

77
00:05:00,917 --> 00:05:03,418
I am going to go and
spread real strength.

78
00:05:03,501 --> 00:05:06,668
The truth as only
death can reveal it!

79
00:05:06,751 --> 00:05:09,001
(Satoru sighs) We just
went over this a minute ago.

80
00:05:09,085 --> 00:05:11,252
Are you a slow learner?

81
00:05:11,335 --> 00:05:13,086
(coughs) This
smoke is so irritating.

82
00:05:16,335 --> 00:05:18,294
What's going on here?

83
00:05:18,378 --> 00:05:19,253
(hums)

84
00:05:19,336 --> 00:05:22,336
In simple terms, you missed me.

85
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:24,670
Impossible, I felt
the contact just now!

86
00:05:24,753 --> 00:05:27,421
I touched you, and not
only that, I killed you!

87
00:05:27,504 --> 00:05:29,421
No, what you actually touched

88
00:05:29,504 --> 00:05:32,295
was the "Infinity" existing
between you and me.

89
00:05:33,588 --> 00:05:34,588
Here, I'll show you.

90
00:05:35,422 --> 00:05:36,630
Put your hand out.

91
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:38,964
(grumbles)

92
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:40,131
Oh, come on!

93
00:05:42,297 --> 00:05:44,381
Come on, come on!

94
00:05:44,464 --> 00:05:46,673
I don't sense
hostility or trickery.

95
00:05:46,756 --> 00:05:48,840
Guess I'll see what it's about.

96
00:05:54,257 --> 00:05:55,924
(gasps)

97
00:05:56,007 --> 00:05:57,092
See?

98
00:05:59,008 --> 00:06:00,341
I can't touch him!

99
00:06:00,425 --> 00:06:02,466
I get stopped just short of him!

100
00:06:02,550 --> 00:06:05,300
Is this Infinity?

101
00:06:05,384 --> 00:06:07,384
Not exactly stopped,

102
00:06:07,467 --> 00:06:10,342
but the closer you
get, the slower you go.

103
00:06:10,426 --> 00:06:12,802
(groans)

104
00:06:12,885 --> 00:06:14,552
So, what now?

105
00:06:14,635 --> 00:06:16,510
We could just hold
hands if you like.

106
00:06:17,677 --> 00:06:19,343
I refuse!

107
00:06:19,427 --> 00:06:20,886
Oh, don't be shy now.

108
00:06:22,095 --> 00:06:24,428
You're making me
feel self-conscious, too!

109
00:06:24,511 --> 00:06:25,511
(growls)

110
00:06:25,594 --> 00:06:27,302
You bastard!

111
00:06:27,386 --> 00:06:30,846
-(punch landing)
-(groans in pain)

112
00:06:30,929 --> 00:06:31,929
(coughs wetly)

113
00:06:31,971 --> 00:06:33,096
So fast!

114
00:06:33,179 --> 00:06:35,220
I don't get it, it's
not just a blow

115
00:06:35,303 --> 00:06:37,346
that's strengthened
with cursed energy!

116
00:06:37,430 --> 00:06:38,555
So, what is it?

117
00:06:38,638 --> 00:06:39,638
I must know!

118
00:06:40,388 --> 00:06:41,930
There's still more!

119
00:06:42,013 --> 00:06:44,389
-(punches landing)
-(grunting in pain)

120
00:06:44,472 --> 00:06:47,514
(screams)

121
00:06:47,597 --> 00:06:50,556
Infinity exists everywhere.

122
00:06:51,806 --> 00:06:54,890
I just use my jujutsu to
bring it forward into reality.

123
00:06:55,765 --> 00:06:58,390
Convergence, divergence.

124
00:06:58,473 --> 00:07:01,142
What do you think happens
when one touches this void?

125
00:07:01,891 --> 00:07:04,558
Cursed Technique Reversal.

126
00:07:04,641 --> 00:07:05,641
Red.

127
00:07:08,059 --> 00:07:10,684
(grunts)

128
00:07:10,767 --> 00:07:13,559
(ground breaking)

129
00:07:13,642 --> 00:07:18,601
-(grunting)
-(trees snapping)

130
00:07:21,309 --> 00:07:24,394
-(yells)
-(punch landing)

131
00:07:24,477 --> 00:07:29,103
-(body thudding)
-(grunting in pain)

132
00:07:29,186 --> 00:07:31,979
(grunting in pain)

133
00:07:39,688 --> 00:07:42,438
(yells battle cry)

134
00:07:45,354 --> 00:07:48,022
-(kick landing)
-(screams)

135
00:07:48,106 --> 00:07:51,022
(body slamming)

136
00:07:51,106 --> 00:07:52,605
Well, that's that.

137
00:07:53,397 --> 00:07:55,565
(rain falling)

138
00:07:55,648 --> 00:07:57,231
[Sugeru] You can try,

139
00:07:57,314 --> 00:07:58,398
but you'll die.

140
00:07:59,398 --> 00:08:00,481
Jougo.

141
00:08:01,857 --> 00:08:04,649
(water splashing)

142
00:08:07,732 --> 00:08:10,482
I guess it wasn't just talk.

143
00:08:10,566 --> 00:08:12,984
(chuckles)

144
00:08:13,067 --> 00:08:14,567
No matter.

145
00:08:14,650 --> 00:08:17,400
If I can't hit him, I'll just
drag him into my Domain.

146
00:08:18,526 --> 00:08:19,860
Wait.

147
00:08:19,943 --> 00:08:21,068
Where'd he go?

148
00:08:22,693 --> 00:08:23,734
Sorry about that.

149
00:08:23,818 --> 00:08:25,276
-Huh?
-Hey, what's going on here?

150
00:08:25,359 --> 00:08:27,527
Where in the hell are
we? How did I get here?

151
00:08:27,610 --> 00:08:28,735
-Sorry.
-I don't get it!

152
00:08:28,819 --> 00:08:30,402
What is this place, hey!

153
00:08:30,485 --> 00:08:31,610
What the hell?

154
00:08:31,694 --> 00:08:33,069
Sukuna's vessel?

155
00:08:33,153 --> 00:08:35,736
To observe, I've
brought Yuuji Itadori.

156
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:36,862
Mount Fuji!

157
00:08:36,945 --> 00:08:38,236
His head's Mount Fuji!

158
00:08:40,736 --> 00:08:43,279
(footsteps tapping)

159
00:08:46,529 --> 00:08:48,237
I aim to protect you!

160
00:08:48,946 --> 00:08:50,447
I'll never leave you!

161
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:53,405
-(snoring)
-[Frodo] Sam.

162
00:08:53,488 --> 00:08:55,822
(Sam sobbing)

163
00:08:58,489 --> 00:08:59,406
Wow.

164
00:08:59,489 --> 00:09:01,448
He learns surprisingly quickly.

165
00:09:02,906 --> 00:09:04,424
-[Frodo] Come on, Sam.
-[Satoru] Yuuji!

166
00:09:04,448 --> 00:09:06,574
(yelps)

167
00:09:06,657 --> 00:09:09,116
Oh hey, so what's up, Gojou?

168
00:09:09,199 --> 00:09:10,967
Talking to him doesn't
cause a problem, either.

169
00:09:10,991 --> 00:09:12,199
You need something?

170
00:09:12,282 --> 00:09:14,159
[Satoru] So we can
increase his output quickly

171
00:09:14,241 --> 00:09:16,283
and move on to
the next stage soon.

172
00:09:16,992 --> 00:09:18,324
We're heading out, let's go.

173
00:09:18,408 --> 00:09:19,533
Huh?

174
00:09:19,616 --> 00:09:20,843
[Satoru] It's a
field trip lesson.

175
00:09:20,867 --> 00:09:23,118
I'm going to teach you
about the very pinnacle

176
00:09:23,201 --> 00:09:24,534
of jujutsu battles.

177
00:09:25,742 --> 00:09:27,034
Domain Expansion.

178
00:09:30,452 --> 00:09:31,368
(water splashing)

179
00:09:31,452 --> 00:09:32,702
What the hell's this?

180
00:09:32,785 --> 00:09:34,285
How come I'm not sinking?

181
00:09:35,577 --> 00:09:39,578
Gojou, I was at the school
just 10 seconds ago, right?

182
00:09:39,661 --> 00:09:40,703
What's going on, here?

183
00:09:40,786 --> 00:09:42,244
Oh, I warped us.

184
00:09:42,327 --> 00:09:43,619
He's not gonna explain it.

185
00:09:43,703 --> 00:09:45,204
Sukuna's vessel!

186
00:09:45,287 --> 00:09:47,328
So he really is alive.

187
00:09:47,412 --> 00:09:48,954
[Suguru] The first thing,

188
00:09:49,037 --> 00:09:52,370
you must somehow render
Satoru Gojou incapable of fighting.

189
00:09:52,454 --> 00:09:56,496
The second is to get Ryoumen
Sukuna and Yuuji Itadori

190
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:58,288
on your side.

191
00:09:58,371 --> 00:10:02,081
I can't kill Itadori because
of our future plans.

192
00:10:02,165 --> 00:10:04,831
Has Gojou figured
out what we're up to?

193
00:10:04,914 --> 00:10:07,539
What'd you bring
the kid for, a shield?

194
00:10:07,622 --> 00:10:08,707
A shield?

195
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:10,498
No, no, I already
explained this.

196
00:10:10,582 --> 00:10:12,498
He's just here to watch.

197
00:10:12,582 --> 00:10:15,540
You see, I'm in the midst of
teaching him a lot of things.

198
00:10:15,623 --> 00:10:18,416
So forget about him
and let's just fight.

199
00:10:19,541 --> 00:10:22,000
Having him tag along with
you isn't gonna slow you down?

200
00:10:22,083 --> 00:10:23,666
It makes you look like an idiot.

201
00:10:23,749 --> 00:10:27,001
Oh, no, it'll all be fine.

202
00:10:27,084 --> 00:10:28,459
I mean, really.

203
00:10:28,542 --> 00:10:30,542
You're kind of weak.

204
00:10:30,625 --> 00:10:32,001
(chuckles)

205
00:10:32,084 --> 00:10:34,418
(growls)

206
00:10:34,501 --> 00:10:35,877
(fire roaring)

207
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,418
How dare you insult me
like that, you insolent ass?

208
00:10:38,501 --> 00:10:41,211
I'm going to enjoy tearing
up that smug face of yours!

209
00:10:42,211 --> 00:10:43,919
(fire exploding)

210
00:10:44,003 --> 00:10:46,627
(water crashing)

211
00:10:48,545 --> 00:10:49,587
This guy

212
00:10:50,295 --> 00:10:51,462
is weak?

213
00:10:53,587 --> 00:10:56,130
He's way more powerful
than any of the monsters

214
00:10:56,213 --> 00:10:57,713
I've encountered so far!

215
00:11:01,130 --> 00:11:02,713
(shudders)

216
00:11:02,796 --> 00:11:03,881
(grunts)

217
00:11:03,964 --> 00:11:05,630
You'll be fine.

218
00:11:05,714 --> 00:11:07,297
Just stay here close to me.

219
00:11:08,922 --> 00:11:11,673
(grunts)

220
00:11:11,756 --> 00:11:13,048
Domain Expansion!

221
00:11:18,132 --> 00:11:20,091
(gasps)

222
00:11:22,716 --> 00:11:25,716
(ground breaking)

223
00:11:28,508 --> 00:11:30,425
(gasps)

224
00:11:32,258 --> 00:11:34,800
(lava bubbling)

225
00:11:36,801 --> 00:11:39,718
(chuckles)

226
00:11:39,801 --> 00:11:40,718
What is this?

227
00:11:40,801 --> 00:11:41,801
Damn!

228
00:11:43,094 --> 00:11:45,719
Coffin of the Iron Mountain!

229
00:11:56,887 --> 00:11:59,387
(lava bubbling)

230
00:11:59,471 --> 00:12:02,554
(lava exploding)

231
00:12:02,637 --> 00:12:03,679
What is this?

232
00:12:03,762 --> 00:12:05,512
Damn!

233
00:12:05,596 --> 00:12:07,305
[Satoru] This is
Domain Expansion.

234
00:12:07,388 --> 00:12:08,638
(chuckles evilly)

235
00:12:08,722 --> 00:12:10,305
The Innate Domain is made

236
00:12:10,388 --> 00:12:11,763
-with cursed energy.
-(yelps)

237
00:12:11,847 --> 00:12:13,805
Then, you imbue it
with a cursed technique.

238
00:12:13,889 --> 00:12:15,890
(blows air rapidly)

239
00:12:15,973 --> 00:12:18,473
What you three encountered
at that juvenile detention center

240
00:12:18,556 --> 00:12:20,681
was an incomplete
Domain that hadn't been

241
00:12:20,764 --> 00:12:22,682
imbued with any
cursed techniques.

242
00:12:22,765 --> 00:12:24,765
If that had been
a proper Domain,

243
00:12:24,849 --> 00:12:26,891
all of you first-years
would have died.

244
00:12:26,974 --> 00:12:28,849
I think Megumi understood that.

245
00:12:30,308 --> 00:12:31,892
Spreading out an
Innate Domain that way

246
00:12:31,975 --> 00:12:34,142
always consumes a ton of energy.

247
00:12:34,225 --> 00:12:36,142
But the advantages
make it worth it.

248
00:12:36,225 --> 00:12:38,018
One of them is
the boost to stats

249
00:12:38,101 --> 00:12:39,934
due to environmental factors.

250
00:12:40,018 --> 00:12:41,350
Ah!

251
00:12:41,434 --> 00:12:43,392
You mean like
buffs in video games!

252
00:12:44,767 --> 00:12:46,102
Another one is...

253
00:12:46,810 --> 00:12:48,643
(rock exploding)

254
00:12:48,727 --> 00:12:49,768
What?

255
00:12:49,852 --> 00:12:51,685
Most sorcerers would
have been burned to ash

256
00:12:51,768 --> 00:12:54,311
the moment they
entered my Domain!

257
00:12:55,228 --> 00:12:56,603
The techniques
imbued in the Domain

258
00:12:56,686 --> 00:12:59,603
are always sure to
hit within that Domain.

259
00:12:59,686 --> 00:13:01,187
That is guaranteed.

260
00:13:01,269 --> 00:13:02,395
Guaranteed?

261
00:13:02,479 --> 00:13:04,353
That's correct!

262
00:13:04,437 --> 00:13:05,770
But don't worry.

263
00:13:05,854 --> 00:13:07,729
There are several
ways to deal with it.

264
00:13:09,813 --> 00:13:11,855
You can take the hit
using a cursed technique,

265
00:13:11,938 --> 00:13:15,646
like just now, or, and I don't
really recommend this one,

266
00:13:15,730 --> 00:13:18,647
but you can try to go
outside the Domain.

267
00:13:18,731 --> 00:13:20,439
That's usually impossible.

268
00:13:20,522 --> 00:13:21,647
Now, you can also-

269
00:13:21,731 --> 00:13:23,772
[Jougo] If I neutralize
that Infinity of yours

270
00:13:23,856 --> 00:13:27,857
with a dense Domain, then
my techniques will reach you.

271
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:29,523
Yeah, they'll hit.

272
00:13:29,607 --> 00:13:30,857
Infinity?

273
00:13:30,940 --> 00:13:32,940
You have to give
me the Prison Realm!

274
00:13:34,566 --> 00:13:35,816
To add to my collection!

275
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:39,108
I came here half in jest,

276
00:13:39,192 --> 00:13:42,151
thinking I wouldn't really
care if I couldn't kill him.

277
00:13:42,234 --> 00:13:44,692
But now, having this
difference between us

278
00:13:44,775 --> 00:13:48,567
thrust in my face,
having him insult my pride

279
00:13:48,650 --> 00:13:52,902
as a cursed spirit,
ridiculing the new humanity,

280
00:13:52,985 --> 00:13:55,443
this is completely unacceptable!

281
00:13:56,986 --> 00:13:59,444
The most effective way
to deal with a Domain

282
00:14:00,736 --> 00:14:02,652
is to lay out your own Domain.

283
00:14:02,736 --> 00:14:05,862
When two Domains are
laid out at the same time,

284
00:14:05,945 --> 00:14:08,778
the more refined one
will dominate that space.

285
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:13,654
Though compatibility and the
amount of energy can factor in.

286
00:14:13,738 --> 00:14:15,238
(foot stomping)

287
00:14:15,321 --> 00:14:17,779
There won't even be ashes
left of you, Satoru Gojou!

288
00:14:19,613 --> 00:14:22,822
(ground breaking)

289
00:14:22,906 --> 00:14:25,614
(Jougo grunts)

290
00:14:25,697 --> 00:14:26,947
Domain Expansion.

291
00:14:30,323 --> 00:14:31,990
Infinite Void.

292
00:14:43,241 --> 00:14:44,867
(crickets chirping)

293
00:14:44,950 --> 00:14:47,950
(water splashing)

294
00:14:56,659 --> 00:14:58,118
[Jougo] What just happened?

295
00:14:59,494 --> 00:15:02,244
Can it be that my
Domain was overwhelmed?

296
00:15:03,452 --> 00:15:04,744
I can't see anything.

297
00:15:05,827 --> 00:15:07,661
I can't feel anything!

298
00:15:08,578 --> 00:15:09,953
No!

299
00:15:10,037 --> 00:15:11,828
I can see everything!

300
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:15,120
I can feel everything!

301
00:15:15,205 --> 00:15:17,704
But the information
is never complete,

302
00:15:17,787 --> 00:15:20,954
so I can't do anything!

303
00:15:22,329 --> 00:15:24,997
This is the inner
world of Limitless.

304
00:15:25,955 --> 00:15:28,705
Perception, contact.

305
00:15:28,788 --> 00:15:33,748
Every act in life is repeated
infinitely, over and over.

306
00:15:34,081 --> 00:15:34,956
(grunts in shock)

307
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:36,873
Ironic, isn't it?

308
00:15:36,956 --> 00:15:40,582
When granted every
possible thing, you can't use it.

309
00:15:40,665 --> 00:15:43,249
All you can do
is die peacefully.

310
00:15:43,332 --> 00:15:45,957
But I have some things
I still want to ask you,

311
00:15:46,041 --> 00:15:48,958
so for right now, I'm
going to let you off the hook

312
00:15:49,042 --> 00:15:50,875
with just this.

313
00:15:50,958 --> 00:15:54,500
(flesh stretching)

314
00:15:54,584 --> 00:15:58,459
-(flesh ripping)
-(blood splattering)

315
00:15:58,542 --> 00:16:00,542
(glass shattering)

316
00:16:00,626 --> 00:16:03,376
(head clattering)

317
00:16:04,627 --> 00:16:06,710
-(foot stomping)
-Now, then.

318
00:16:06,793 --> 00:16:09,169
Just who instructed
you to come after me?

319
00:16:10,503 --> 00:16:14,003
He really is the
strongest jujutsu sorcerer!

320
00:16:14,086 --> 00:16:15,586
As a living organism,

321
00:16:15,669 --> 00:16:17,003
he's on another level!

322
00:16:20,670 --> 00:16:21,754
[Sugeru] Oh dear.

323
00:16:23,087 --> 00:16:24,587
What now?

324
00:16:24,670 --> 00:16:26,379
Will you rescue him?

325
00:16:26,463 --> 00:16:29,505
I can't let any of the people
from the school see my face,

326
00:16:29,588 --> 00:16:31,713
so I'll be leaving here now.

327
00:16:31,796 --> 00:16:34,339
I trust you to finish this.

328
00:16:35,714 --> 00:16:39,006
If you want to save him,
then go ahead and save him.

329
00:16:39,089 --> 00:16:42,465
Though I don't know, do your
kind have sentimental emotions?

330
00:16:43,381 --> 00:16:46,548
(distorted backwards speech)

331
00:16:46,632 --> 00:16:49,883
(footsteps tapping)

332
00:16:49,966 --> 00:16:53,050
That's quite a statement
for a cursed spirit to make.

333
00:16:54,258 --> 00:16:56,925
You don't seem like
the type to follow orders.

334
00:16:57,008 --> 00:17:00,218
Was something good supposed
to happen if you killed me?

335
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:03,009
Regardless, you're
going to have to tell me.

336
00:17:03,092 --> 00:17:04,634
Who sent you?

337
00:17:04,717 --> 00:17:06,010
I want a name.

338
00:17:07,219 --> 00:17:09,010
Come on, just tell me already.

339
00:17:09,093 --> 00:17:10,260
(grunts in pain)

340
00:17:10,343 --> 00:17:13,093
Like I'd ever tell
you, you little punk!

341
00:17:13,178 --> 00:17:14,928
What a bad attitude.

342
00:17:15,011 --> 00:17:16,677
And you're so compromised!

343
00:17:16,761 --> 00:17:17,802
(grunts in pain)

344
00:17:17,886 --> 00:17:19,094
Damn you!

345
00:17:19,178 --> 00:17:22,512
If you don't tell
me, I'll exorcise you.

346
00:17:22,595 --> 00:17:24,012
Though I will anyway.

347
00:17:24,095 --> 00:17:25,470
So weird!

348
00:17:25,553 --> 00:17:27,303
Curses are capable
of conversations?

349
00:17:27,386 --> 00:17:29,013
Here, it almost seems normal.

350
00:17:30,263 --> 00:17:32,096
(ground slamming)

351
00:17:32,180 --> 00:17:33,888
-(grunts in shock)
-(gasps)

352
00:17:33,971 --> 00:17:36,847
(flowers rustling)

353
00:17:37,555 --> 00:17:38,555
Aww!

354
00:17:38,639 --> 00:17:40,056
-So pretty!
-Flowers!

355
00:17:40,139 --> 00:17:41,056
(grunts in confusion)

356
00:17:41,139 --> 00:17:42,264
(laughs joyously)

357
00:17:42,347 --> 00:17:43,264
-(grunts)
-(hand slapping)

358
00:17:43,347 --> 00:17:44,681
It's just a curse!

359
00:17:44,765 --> 00:17:47,182
And it's stripping
away my will to fight!

360
00:17:47,265 --> 00:17:49,431
(screams)

361
00:17:53,557 --> 00:17:54,474
Leave me, Gojou!

362
00:17:54,557 --> 00:17:57,141
Go after them, I'll be fine!

363
00:17:57,225 --> 00:17:59,058
(screams)

364
00:17:59,141 --> 00:18:00,307
Wait, forget that, I lied!

365
00:18:00,391 --> 00:18:01,184
I need help!

366
00:18:01,267 --> 00:18:03,059
(blade slicing)

367
00:18:03,142 --> 00:18:06,808
-(fire roaring)
-(grunts in pain)

368
00:18:06,892 --> 00:18:08,268
(hums in admiration)

369
00:18:08,351 --> 00:18:09,976
He got away.

370
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:12,101
He's good at
hiding his presence.

371
00:18:13,227 --> 00:18:16,102
He's way more impressive
than Volcano Head.

372
00:18:18,061 --> 00:18:20,102
(flowers rustling)

373
00:18:20,186 --> 00:18:21,310
I'm sorry about that.

374
00:18:21,393 --> 00:18:22,753
So now cursed
spirits of that level

375
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:24,978
-are joining forces?
-But then you're the one

376
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:26,871
-who brought me here.
-It's getting interesting!

377
00:18:26,895 --> 00:18:28,062
Yuuji!

378
00:18:28,145 --> 00:18:30,311
I want you, as well as
all of your classmates,

379
00:18:30,394 --> 00:18:33,104
to become strong enough
that you can beat that.

380
00:18:33,188 --> 00:18:35,146
Me, beat that?

381
00:18:35,230 --> 00:18:36,854
It's better to have
a concrete goal,

382
00:18:36,938 --> 00:18:38,188
wouldn't you say?

383
00:18:38,271 --> 00:18:40,939
Man, I'm glad I
brought you today!

384
00:18:41,022 --> 00:18:42,396
Is he serious?

385
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:45,105
I've had no idea what was
going on this whole time!

386
00:18:45,189 --> 00:18:46,855
Now that we've set you a goal,

387
00:18:46,939 --> 00:18:49,523
all that's left is to pursue
it and then attain it.

388
00:18:49,606 --> 00:18:51,356
Let's speed up your schedule.

389
00:18:51,439 --> 00:18:54,065
For the next month, you'll
still be watching movies,

390
00:18:54,148 --> 00:18:56,024
but you'll also be
fighting against me.

391
00:18:56,107 --> 00:18:57,899
Fighting with you?

392
00:18:57,982 --> 00:18:59,315
(groans dejectedly)

393
00:18:59,398 --> 00:19:01,815
Will I still even be alive
after a month of that?

394
00:19:01,899 --> 00:19:03,525
Then it's combat training.

395
00:19:03,608 --> 00:19:06,358
You'll be sent out on
more difficult missions.

396
00:19:06,441 --> 00:19:08,566
The basics and
how to apply them.

397
00:19:08,650 --> 00:19:11,151
And then finally, you can
show off all these new skills

398
00:19:11,235 --> 00:19:12,692
at the Exchange Event!

399
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:13,859
Wait, teacher!

400
00:19:13,943 --> 00:19:14,859
Yes?

401
00:19:14,943 --> 00:19:15,859
And what's your question?

402
00:19:15,943 --> 00:19:18,567
The Exchange Event is what?

403
00:19:18,651 --> 00:19:20,277
(grunts questioningly)

404
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:21,818
[Satoru] I didn't tell you?

405
00:19:23,152 --> 00:19:24,610
(growls)

406
00:19:24,693 --> 00:19:26,069
(stammers)

407
00:19:26,152 --> 00:19:27,611
(growls)

408
00:19:27,694 --> 00:19:30,111
(stammers)

409
00:19:30,195 --> 00:19:31,402
He's late!

410
00:19:31,486 --> 00:19:33,444
(yelps)

411
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:38,279
(footsteps tapping)

412
00:19:43,655 --> 00:19:47,155
(door creaking)

413
00:19:47,239 --> 00:19:49,655
(door closing)

414
00:19:51,697 --> 00:19:55,240
(door creaking)

415
00:19:55,322 --> 00:19:58,073
(water splashing)

416
00:20:00,282 --> 00:20:03,074
[Suguru] Sure is peaceful here.

417
00:20:06,324 --> 00:20:08,200
How's Jougo doing, Getou?

418
00:20:09,242 --> 00:20:10,242
Death's door.

419
00:20:11,324 --> 00:20:13,075
Hanami wants to
save him, though,

420
00:20:13,158 --> 00:20:15,243
so he'll probably be fine.

421
00:20:15,325 --> 00:20:17,325
How irresponsible.

422
00:20:17,408 --> 00:20:19,117
And you're the one
who egged him on.

423
00:20:19,201 --> 00:20:20,492
Heavens, no.

424
00:20:20,575 --> 00:20:21,825
I tried to stop him.

425
00:20:22,618 --> 00:20:25,244
(door creaking)

426
00:20:26,202 --> 00:20:27,743
[Mahito] Speak of the devil.

427
00:20:27,826 --> 00:20:30,036
Jougo, Hanami!

428
00:20:30,119 --> 00:20:32,245
Glad to see you're okay.

429
00:20:32,327 --> 00:20:34,661
How the hell can you
look at me like this

430
00:20:34,744 --> 00:20:36,327
and say I'm okay?

431
00:20:37,245 --> 00:20:39,370
You're lucky that
you got off so easy.

432
00:20:39,453 --> 00:20:40,703
(growls)

433
00:20:40,787 --> 00:20:41,620
(hums mockingly)

434
00:20:41,703 --> 00:20:42,995
Why, you...

435
00:20:43,079 --> 00:20:45,579
[Suguru] Maybe now
at least you understand.

436
00:20:45,663 --> 00:20:47,788
So we'll go about
sealing Satoru Gojou

437
00:20:47,871 --> 00:20:50,663
at the appropriate time,
in the appropriate place,

438
00:20:50,746 --> 00:20:52,955
once we've secured
our advantage over him.

439
00:20:54,081 --> 00:20:57,330
D-Day is October
31st in Shibuya.

440
00:20:57,413 --> 00:20:59,248
Later, I'll have more details.

441
00:21:00,497 --> 00:21:02,290
Good, Mahito?

442
00:21:04,998 --> 00:21:06,790
No objections.

443
00:21:06,873 --> 00:21:08,165
Let's be cunning,

444
00:21:09,250 --> 00:21:10,999
as curses should.

445
00:21:11,083 --> 00:21:12,291
And humans should.

446
00:21:13,374 --> 00:21:15,624
(chuckles)

447
00:21:15,707 --> 00:21:20,667
(Closing Theme Music)

448
00:21:22,917 --> 00:21:27,876
(singing in Japanese)

449
00:22:44,970 --> 00:22:47,011
(playful music)

450
00:22:47,386 --> 00:22:48,262
[Both] One!

451
00:22:48,344 --> 00:22:49,344
Two and!

452
00:22:49,427 --> 00:22:50,594
Three and!

453
00:22:50,678 --> 00:22:52,470
-Four and!
-What the hell are you doing?

454
00:22:52,554 --> 00:22:53,470
We're warming up.

455
00:22:53,554 --> 00:22:55,137
[Both] Six and!

456
00:22:55,221 --> 00:22:56,845
I think I'm warmed up enough.

457
00:22:56,929 --> 00:22:58,012
Me, too.

458
00:22:59,054 --> 00:23:00,180
(hums questioningly)

459
00:23:00,264 --> 00:23:01,846
What exactly are
you warming up for?

460
00:23:01,930 --> 00:23:03,721
-(whistle blowing)
-(grunts)

461
00:23:03,805 --> 00:23:04,846
(screams)

462
00:23:04,930 --> 00:23:07,389
(lively music)

463
00:23:11,139 --> 00:23:12,847
(panting)

464
00:23:12,931 --> 00:23:13,931
Getou, cross!

465
00:23:13,973 --> 00:23:14,764
(screams)

466
00:23:14,848 --> 00:23:15,890
Thanks!

467
00:23:15,974 --> 00:23:17,723
-Shoot!
-(screams)

468
00:23:17,807 --> 00:23:21,266
(grunts in pain)

469
00:23:21,348 --> 00:23:23,058
Mahito, here!

470
00:23:23,141 --> 00:23:25,308
(screams)

471
00:23:27,432 --> 00:23:28,516
Overhead

472
00:23:29,808 --> 00:23:31,475
bicycle kick!

473
00:23:33,142 --> 00:23:35,184
(screams)

474
00:23:38,434 --> 00:23:41,685
(whistle blowing)

475
00:23:41,768 --> 00:23:45,434
I'm gonna kill these
two for this later!

476
00:23:45,518 --> 00:23:48,061
(intense music)

